WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.667
-I'm so happy to see you
in person.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.400
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.667
-I am so happy to be here again.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.901
Like, one year --
almost two years.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.834
-Yeah, right?

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:11.968
Here's what happened
since I last talked to you.

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.868
-Okay.
-Ready for this?

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:17.601
Your song "Tusa" hit one billion
streams on Spotify.

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:19.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.100
One billion.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:28.801
Your album "KG0516" went to
number one on the albums charts.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:31.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:34.167
Right now you're in the middle
of a soldout tour.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:39.033
And finally, last night
you won another Latin Grammy

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.767
for Best Reggaeton Performance!

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.100
♪♪

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.067
♪♪

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.400
-Ah, ah, ah.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.868
Have to bring you to Colombia.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.467
Those steps, those steps.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:04.334
-I don't know if they'll allow
Grandpa into Colombia.

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:06.501
But anyway.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.534
You're obviously from Colombia.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:12.234
But before that, you also -- you
lived in New York for a while.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.667
-I lived in New York.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:16.501
You know, like, I came to
New York for one thing.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:19.100
-What?
-I wanted to stop doing music.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.934
So I moved to New York.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.100
-To stop doing music?
-To stop doing music.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.067
-And then what made you
start doing the music?

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.634
-I had to --
I used to live in Baldwin.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.868
So I had to take three buses
and one train

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:34.400
to get to my school
in Manhattan.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.334
And then in the train
all the time,

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.400
I was watching, like,
a billboard of music conference.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.834
And it says like,
"Music but in business,"

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.334
like in a business point.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:46.734
So every day I was
in the train like, "Why?

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.534
If I want to stop doing music,

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:51.968
I have to see these people
every...day!"

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:56.100
-So you kept seeing music,
music, music every day.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.567
-Yeah.
-And you knew that's a sign.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:01.234
-I went to Boston and I studied
that and I'm here, you know?

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.767
-Look at you now.
Yeah, look at you now.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.000
Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.501
-I'm back into music
and I'm here again.

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.334
-Congrats.
You're on your solo tour.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.300
How does that feel
to have your own tour?

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.234
-Like, it's something --
I don't know.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.400
I'm telling my people
all the time, like,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.033
I'm in an airplane mode
because --

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:19.868
it's hard to believe --

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.501
When I'm out,
it's hard to believe that

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:25.133
all of those thousand people
are there for me.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.868
It's amazing.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.934
-And being part of
those people's lives,

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.334
it's amazing for me.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:34.200
We started, like,
selling theaters,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.400
and then it became,
like, so huge,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.033
and people started buying a lot,

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:42.634
so we moved from theaters
to the arenas right now.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:43.834
So I'm happy.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.434
People, I love you so much

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:49.300
for giving me this amazing
moment in my career!

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.100
-Do you look into the crowd

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.334
and just see, like,
a sea of blue hair?

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:54.767
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.367
No, yeah.
-That's good.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.968
-You're laughing but it's true.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.968
Like, I go out
and it's like a --

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:03.100
I don't know -- like a big,
blue cloud in the crowd.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.767
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.634
-They use wigs and they put,
like, all of my tattoos.

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.367
And they have their merch.
It's amazing.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.767
I love that, people.
It's everything.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.300
-Can you explain what
"bichota" is?

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.567
-Bichota? Oh, my God. Okay.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:18.200
I'm going to -- I'm going to
say it because --

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.334
I'm going to say it. Bichota.

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:23.767
It's a word that I knew
from Puerto Rican friends.

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:24.901
-Yeah.

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:28.100
-The meaning is "drug dealer,"
"bichote."

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.467
It's the head of the drugs.
Okay.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.267
So the word for me -- Okay.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.634
So, the word for me, like,
the meaning was, I know, tough.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.100
But for me, the word,
it's, like, powerful.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.400
So I said, "What about bichota?"

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.834
"No bichota, they don't use it.
They use bichote."

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:45.100
"No, I wanted bichota."

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.167
I wanted to create a bichota,

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.000
but the meaning is going to be,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.901
like, a like a boss bitch girl,
powerful, great...

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:54.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
...amazing,

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.634
doing her things by herself,
you know?

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:59.167
-So, bichota -- So you go,
"I'm making a new thing.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.934
I'm making a --"
-Trying.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.534
-And then you put -- You didn't
even try. You succeeded,

00:04:03.534 --> 00:04:05.200
because the song became
a giant hit.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.701
-You know what happened
yesterday?

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:09.634
We were in -- I was in
the concert, in my concert.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:12.300
And I was about to perform
"Bichota."

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.000
So, in the ear, my team told me
like, "Hey, Karol.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.267
You just like five minutes
before, you just won the Grammy,

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.501
the Latin Grammy for 'Bichota.'"

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.200
So I was about to perform
"Bichota"

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.634
and I started screaming.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.367
I told all of my people like,
"Hey, now we have a Grammy."

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:33.367
And we performed "Bichota."
It was amazing. Wow, amazing.

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.767
-Look at you.
You're doing it all.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.968
You're doing it.
It's all happening.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:40.701
It's all real!
-I'm happy, happy for that.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:43.801
-I know you're so young,
but I just want to ask.

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.434
Do you want to
just keep doing this?

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.734
Do you want to do other things?
You have other interests?

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:49.934
Or is this it?
You like, "No, this is --"

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:51.200
-I don't know.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.200
I have a lot of things that
I want to do in my life.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.133
I just want to push myself
and see, as a woman,

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:59.968
how far I can go in everything.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:02.567
Like, in business way,
maybe acting.

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.300
I'm going to act.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.901
You know, I have a surprise
for my people in January.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:10.334
I'm going to start, like,
shooting a series for Netflix.

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.267
It's not about my life.
It's acting.

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:15.400
Like, I have a character, so I'm
preparing myself for that.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.234
-In January?
-In January.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.734
-[ Gasps ] On Netflix?

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.033
Come on, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:22.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.767
The sky's the limit.
The sky's the limit.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.000
Always good to see you.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.167
Karol G right there.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.501
-Thank you, everybody.

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:33.300
Go to karolgmusic.com
for more info on her tour!

